#{[17592186505723 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186505244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505723 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186505362 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505723 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186505396 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505723 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186505477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505723 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186505509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505723 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505723 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505723 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186505477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505723 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f6e1f623-bd44-5493-8260-283c244d07a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505754 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186505723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505754 #edb/ref 1069 "q-38110" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505754 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505754 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If $\\text{Im}(T)=\\{[x,y,z]^{T}\\,:\\,y=z\\}$ then $\\text{nullity}(T)=1$\n\nII. If $Tx=[1,-2,3]^{T}$ has no solution, then $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$\n\nIII. If $\\text{Im}(T)=\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]\\}$, then $T$ is invertible" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505754 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "31c1a37a-969b-5cd4-b27b-164fe43832ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505754 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $T$ is a linear transformation from ${R}^{3}$ into ${R}^{3},$ the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n $T$ is a bijection (an invertible transformation) $\\,⟺\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=3 \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)+\\text{nullity}(T)=3.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $y=z,$ any vector from $\\text{Im}(T)$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=x{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{1}}+z{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that $\\text{Im}(T)=\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}.$ Therefore, $\\text{rank}(T)=2.$ Finally, according to the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T) & =3-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =3-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $Tx=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ has no solution, this means that $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\notin \\text{Im}(T).$ Therefore, $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{3}$ and, according to the invertible matrix theorem, $\\text{nullity}(T)\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that $\\text{Im}(T)=\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]\\}=\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\}.$ Therefore, $\\text{rank}(T)=1.$ So, $T$ is not a bijection or, which is the same, $T$ is not invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505848 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "04cb0c84-a155-5f7d-84eb-582ddec2e63e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505848 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186365087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505854 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186505875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505854 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1c8b644d-c1aa-5054-80bb-2094a58661c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505854 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186366441 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505856 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186505854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505856 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "29152df7-9145-56fd-81cf-7990f5f65284" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505856 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186366427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505869 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186505856 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505869 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "58501b2a-32e9-5f10-a02d-62409c76c2b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505869 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186505754 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505875 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186505848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505875 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7cd92d7a-8193-53d1-bf92-9e1fa1598872" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505875 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186406840 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
